    "title": "IU Health Set To Break Ground On New Hospital In West Lafayette, Indiana - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Robert McCune ,\n12 hours ago Indiana University Health (IU Health; Indianapolis) is set to break ground this summer on a new hospital in West Lafayette, Ind., according to the Lafayette Journal & Courier. The $214 million full-service hospital will comprise 12 inpatient beds, an emergency department (ED) with 14 treatment spaces and a dedicated trauma care room, four operating room (OR) suites, and an imaging department. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
